{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170765-matter-question","id":1170765,"title":"Matter question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-26T14:06:23-08:00","id":1170765,"title":"Matter question","content":"So, according to game, you need Matter 2 to transmute a substance into another substance, but Matter 3 to reshape it. This means I need Matter 2 to turn lead into gold, but Matter 3 to turn a lead ball into a lead disk. This seems...somewhat off to me. It also seems to break a sort of pattern - transforming simple forces is Forces 3, transforming simple lifeforms is Life 3, transforming simple substances is Matter 2. It's just kind of a wrong note, in my mind.<br /> <br /> Do you suppose there is a really good, game-based reason for this? Do you think it would be particularly game-breaking to switch the two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T15:52:07-08:00","id":1170789,"title":"","content":"It actually makes much more sense than it may first appear.<br /> <br /> With Matter 2, you can transmute things into other things with the following exceptions:<br /> <br /> A: You cannot change state (solid to liquid is not possible)<br /> B: You cannot change dimension (If it starts small, it stays small, and if it started big then there's no shrinking it)<br /> C: You cannot change structure (It's an all or nothing deal. you can't make many layered complicated things, no alloys, tempered glass, radioactive isotopes, or intricate circuitry for you.<br /> <br /> There is a way around B though. It's a rote called &quot;mould and reform&quot;. Let's say you have your lead ball, you can transform it into clay, use your hands to shape it into a disc, and then turn it back to lead again.<br /> <br /> Regarding the progression, it makes a lot of sense to me.<br /> <br /> Matter 1: This is lead<br /> Matter 2: The lead is now gold<br /> Matter 3: The gold is now fog<br /> Matter 4: The fog is now gun<br /> Matter 5: The gun literally shoots bullets made of sunshine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-26-2017, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T17:22:48-08:00","id":1170811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170765-matter-question#post1170765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, according to game, you need Matter 2 to transmute a substance into another substance, but Matter 3 to reshape it. This means I need Matter 2 to turn lead into gold, but Matter 3 to turn a lead ball into a lead disk. This seems...somewhat off to me. It also seems to break a sort of pattern - transforming simple forces is Forces 3, transforming simple lifeforms is Life 3, transforming simple substances is Matter 2. It's just kind of a wrong note, in my mind.<br /> <br /> Do you suppose there is a really good, game-based reason for this? Do you think it would be particularly game-breaking to switch the two?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct. It's out of step with the standard progression that works as the underlying structure of Mage magic. Except where it doesn't, of course. And most of the exceptions are legacies from prior iterations of the game that weren't corrected with edition progression. (White Wolf is worse than many RPGs with how mistakes are recognized and corrected as the games progress and evolve and Mage is the worst amongst those that have had such progression. With M20 being the worst of the worst in the &quot;please everyone by keeping everything&quot; idea). <br /> <br /> It's not game breaking at all. In fact, a quick riff on Saikou's iterations show how un-game breaking it is:<br /> <br /> Matter 1: This is water in liquid form. That ice is water in solid form. That fog is water in gaseous form. <br /> Matter 2: The water is now ice. The ice is now fog. The fog is now water. Or it's ice. (But, without Forces 2, that room temperature ice is going to be water again pretty soon.... And room temperature ice might just be vulgar....). [Probably some simple shaping here.]<br /> Matter 3: That ice is now dry ice or C4. That fog is now mustard gas or nitrous oxide. The water is now acid or alcohol or Pepsi. With a bit more oomph, that liquid Pepsi is now solid C4. Or that lead is now gold. (Congrats! You have already surpassed medieval alchemy as an also-ran Disciple!). [Cooler more complicated shaping in play now.] <br /> Matter 4: The water is now a fully automatic AR-15 with Dragon's Breath ammunition. [Now you can change a lot of fiddly bits all at once and organize them however.]<br /> (I'd start allowing low grade &quot;impossible&quot; matter here...]<br /> Matter 5: Full on impossible matter here, aka Primium, adamantium, orichalcum, cerametal composite, organic-analogue steel. (I'd think that guns that shoot sunshine would take some Forces. Otherwise you get full on Sphere crossover. Why not make it a gun that shoots sunshine, love and eliminates the concept of war?)<br /> <br /> Never underestimate the power of even low level Spheres. If your Practice allows it, even Matter 2 can make any gun non-functional by changing the barrel into mild steel. And you might be able to move things through several transformations to get what you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T18:09:58-08:00","id":1170820,"title":"","content":"To expand on Saikou's point, once you're able to change a material's shape, you get into the area of being able to use it offensively. Like, for instance, causing the concrete in a road to turn into a jutting spike that impales your enemies. Making it Matter 3 to do this would make it consistent with other Spheres, which usually only allow one to start really hurting people at rank 3. At least directly. Matter 2 could be used to turn the air in a room into a noxious or flammable gas...just like Forces 2 could conceivably invert the pull of gravity on a person and make them crack their head open on the ceiling. Or Prime 2 could be used to &quot;rub the bones&quot;. The Sphere ranks seem to be ordered around the level of control over the patterns in question, and how readily they can be weaponized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T18:48:49-08:00","id":1170829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170765-matter-question?p=1170811#post1170811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are correct. It's out of step with the standard progression that works as the underlying structure of Mage magic. Except where it doesn't, of course. And most of the exceptions are legacies from prior iterations of the game that weren't corrected with edition progression. (White Wolf is worse than many RPGs with how mistakes are recognized and corrected as the games progress and evolve and Mage is the worst amongst those that have had such progression. With M20 being the worst of the worst in the &quot;please everyone by keeping everything&quot; idea).<br /> <br /> It's not game breaking at all. In fact, a quick riff on Saikou's iterations show how un-game breaking it is:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I think on further thought, I will switch the two for purposes of my game: changing shape requires only Matter 2, changing material or state requires Matter 3.<br /> <br /> Thanks folks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T09:31:34-08:00","id":1170971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170765-matter-question?p=1170820#post1170820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To expand on Saikou's point, once you're able to change a material's shape, you get into the area of being able to use it offensively. Like, for instance, causing the concrete in a road to turn into a jutting spike that impales your enemies. Making it Matter 3 to do this would make it consistent with other Spheres, which usually only allow one to start really hurting people at rank 3. At least directly. Matter 2 could be used to turn the air in a room into a noxious or flammable gas...just like Forces 2 could conceivably invert the pull of gravity on a person and make them crack their head open on the ceiling. Or Prime 2 could be used to &quot;rub the bones&quot;. The Sphere ranks seem to be ordered around the level of control over the patterns in question, and how readily they can be weaponized.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems like changing all the air in a room into mustard gas is probably a worse thing than making concrete spiky. (Though, I mean, c'mon, lets REALLY get nasty and, say, turn the lenses in someone's classes into spikes that go into their eyes....) <br /> <br /> With the &quot;mostly all or nothing&quot; aspect of using just Arete for casting rolls, it's not going to be that hard to do either one (and also do pathetic minimal amounts of damage either way.... )<br /> <br /> And orienting the totality of progression on the ability to use the Sphere to do damage seems like it should be, ummmm..... on the list of concerns, but, probably not the top one. (As the fact that really the first actual level of Matter warrants thread after thread on its economy destroying potential, and so on...) And, considering how Mage magic works, it's pretty much possible to weaponize ANYTHING. Second spell anyone attempted in our 1st 1st ed. Mage game was &quot;I turn all his intestinal bacteria into scorpions. That's what Life 2 says I can do, right?&quot; and there wasn't much around then to say why that would NOT work and be very very nasty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T16:39:36-08:00","id":1171366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170765-matter-question?p=1170971#post1170971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It seems like changing all the air in a room into mustard gas is probably a worse thing than making concrete spiky. (Though, I mean, c'mon, lets REALLY get nasty and, say, turn the lenses in someone's classes into spikes that go into their eyes....)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to start transmuting air into harmful gas (a personal favourite of mine was Chlorine), then you better have a few dots in Forces if you don't want to engulf yourself in a cloud of deadly poison long before it has a chance to disperse itself towards the enemy.<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, if you're going to start messing about with the spheres, make sure all your players know about this BEFORE they start making characters, and be very very clear about what is and isn't effected by the change. Nothing starts arguments faster than badly communicated changes to assumed rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-31-2017, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T09:39:55-08:00","id":1171548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170765-matter-question?p=1171366#post1171366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're going to start transmuting air into harmful gas (a personal favourite of mine what Chlorine), then you better have a few dots in Forces if you don't want to engulf yourself in a cloud of deadly poison long before it has a chance to disperse itself towards the enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;Shrug&gt; One would assume a mage who can do such a thing would have prepared for it. Forces would be convenient, but not even close to necessary. Having a gas mask would ameliorate the problem (and making sure your friends are in the know and have theirs too). Even, with some poisonous gases (e.g. the ones you should use unless you DO have the necessary Forces to blow it away, Life to make it a non-factor, Entropy &lt;ick&gt; to just luck out of it, etc... and that's if you're not just using a Correspondence window to project the effect), knowing what's coming and being able to take a deep breath and have a planned escape out of the affected area is pretty much all you'll need. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170765-matter-question?p=1171366#post1171366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, if you're going to start messing about with the spheres, make sure all your players know about this BEFORE they start making characters, and be very very clear about what is and isn't effected by the change. Nothing starts arguments faster than badly communicated changes to assumed rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But how is that different from ANY Mage game. There aren't any standard or assumed rules. Tons of choices have to be made in the hard coded crunch on which Purple Boxes are in play and which aren't. And that's not even touching on how the game is going to actually USE the Rules. Is it a Sphere-intense HDYDT mileu? Or is it more free-form? How is your HAP/blah blah blah set up? And are the Purple Boxes selected going to back that up? Even if you aren't using a single Purple Box, you are going to have to make sure everyone KNOWS what is not in play, particularly anyone who has ever played any previous edition of Mage (or even anyone who has read the M20 book) out to anyone who has played any other White Wolf games. Trying to make things logically internally consistent in light of the way magic is supposed to work in one's own game isn't that much of a difference, <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T09:31:07-08:00","id":1171811,"title":"","content":"I mean, letting people know about changes is true for any game. That's just common courtesy.<br /> <br /> Air into poison gas is really just one example, really. I'm sure a significantly clever player could think of many more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T12:03:49-08:00","id":1171846,"title":"","content":"My standard House Rules document for a Mage game runs several pages even if we are trying to hew as close as possible to M20 RAW. Just to define which Purple Boxes we're using and so on. Usually it's substantially longer depending on what the game in question is going to be about. For our next game, an Initiates game as Awakened Orphans without any Sectarian meddling, it's STILL going to be long even with trimming off huge chunks of the game fluff and crunch, just to get the Purple Boxes down + the new House Rules requires to handle how Initiates and M20 are going to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T12:07:35-08:00","id":1172041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170765-matter-question?p=1171811#post1171811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, letting people know about changes is true for any game. That's just common courtesy.<br /> <br /> Air into poison gas is really just one example, really. I'm sure a significantly clever player could think of many more.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sanctum's air into breathable gelatine.<br /> Practice your maniacal cackle and be right in the centre of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T12:36:16-08:00","id":1172049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170765-matter-question?p=1171846#post1171846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My standard House Rules document for a Mage game runs several pages even if we are trying to hew as close as possible to M20 RAW. Just to define which Purple Boxes we're using and so on. Usually it's substantially longer depending on what the game in question is going to be about. For our next game, an Initiates game as Awakened Orphans without any Sectarian meddling, it's STILL going to be long even with trimming off huge chunks of the game fluff and crunch, just to get the Purple Boxes down + the new House Rules requires to handle how Initiates and M20 are going to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never needed such a document. My games tend to run on &quot;As long as the player can convince me something they're doing makes sense and fits in with their character, I'll allow the roll&quot;. And I always have the right to say previous decisions turned out to be a mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-31-2017, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T19:56:48-08:00","id":1172139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1170765-matter-question?p=1172049#post1172049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never needed such a document. My games tend to run on &quot;As long as the player can convince me something they're doing makes sense and fits in with their character, I'll allow the roll&quot;. And I always have the right to say previous decisions turned out to be a mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is really great for the loud and in your face players and will drive away people who don't want to compete. And is fine for the people who are fast thinkers and great bullshit artists, but sucks for people who are more thoughtful and those who want to work from first principles in a straightforward fashion instead of getting by on being persuasive.<br /> <br /> See... that's what rules are FOR. They set up an even table for everyone. Otherwise the game can be, no WILL be, the people who can shout their way to the top of the pile and the people who are okay with them doing that. With a lot of people stalking, walking or slipping away over time. <br /> <br /> Oh, and it can lead to sloppy Storytelling and to playing favorites without even knowing it. It's why all to many games using Fate or the Amber Diceless Engine can end up being &quot;who can flim-flam the ST best&quot;. (And, oh yeah, have I ever been the player doing the flim-flaming, consciously and un...)<br /> <br /> If you never had to deal with these things, great. Though, probably, unless you haven't played very much or only have played with the exact same people from the get go, this HAS been happening whether you knew it or not. It's one of the reasons that a lot of people HATE Mage. The rules are amazingly easy to abuse and subvert. TBH, the &quot;as long as the player can convince me&quot; seems problematic to me, as it implies there are some players who can't and, with the decisions being completely arbitrary and not subject to being graded against any objective criteria... That can be bad. Rules are good for games the same reasons written laws are good for societies. They force fairness and discourage arbitrary application of power. That's also why both can be BAD things in both cases as well. There are games that are choked to death by rules like there are definitely systems of written laws out there that are not so workable, but still both are better than NO accountability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T06:14:15-08:00","id":1172236,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s kinda why I don\u2019t make radical changes to the rules. And the simple rule of law is if the player doesn\u2019t respect me as an authority on the matter, then they are in no ways obligated to continue the game I set up for them.<br /> <br /> Anyone trying to \u201cwin\u201d my games has already missed the point of them, and if that\u2019s the only reason they wish to play, then it\u2019s probably best for us both that we part ways.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m not interested in getting into a ST contest with you. I\u2019m sure your way works for you and your players. There\u2019s no reason to insinuate I am not as capable as you simply because I don\u2019t follow your methods though. That was rather uncalled for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-01-2018, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}